  abstract = {We have investigated the influence of a driving force on the elastic coupling (Labusch parameter) of the field-cooled state of the flux line lattice (FLL) in 400 nm thick YBa\$\_2\$Cu\$\_3\$O\$\_7\$ superconducting films. We found that the FLL of a field-cooled state without driving forces is not in an equilibrium state. Results obtained for magnetic fields applied at \$0\textasciicircum\textbackslash circ\$ and 30\$\textasciicircum\textbackslash circ\$ relative to CuO\$\_2\$ planes, show an enhancement of the elastic coupling of the films at driving current densities several orders of magnitude smaller than the critical one. Our results indicate that the FLL appears to be in a relatively ordered, metastable state after field cooling without driving forces.},
